          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The observation of a group of bright points (around twenty) silently crossing the sky in a few minutes at 10:35 PM, on a weekend night, strongly suggests Thai lanterns, likely released nearby after a private party. The movement is observed from South to North. At 10:00 PM, an east wind is reported in Lyon-Bron: Weather. However, a very light west wind with high variability is noted in Macon: Weather. Since Gleizé is located between these two weather stations, it's difficult to confirm the Thai lantern hypothesis based on wind direction. Nevertheless, the witness's description and the number of observed lights leave little doubt about the phenomenon's origin. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\", a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
